{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "SwiftInbox External Developer API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "Public, developer-facing API for disposable mailboxes, messages, attachments, and webhooks.\n\nEvery endpoint under `/api/v1/*` is protected by an API key (`RequireAPIKey`) and passes through the usage metering middleware (`WithUsage`).\n\n## Authentication\n\nAPI keys are issued to developer accounts and created in the developer dashboard (**Api keys** page). Authenticate every request by sending the key as a Bearer token:\n\n```\nAuthorization: Bearer dev_<64 hex characters>\n```\n\nKeys are validated against their SHA-256 hash server-side. A missing, malformed, unknown, or revoked key returns `401 Unauthorized`. The middleware also accepts the legacy `Authentication: Bearer <key>` header.\n\n> Example values in this specification are illustrative. Substitute your own API key when using **Authorize** / Try it out.\n\n## Usage metering\n\nEvery `/api/v1/*` request records usage against the developer account and the specific API key used. If the developer's monthly quota is exceeded the request is rejected with `429 Too Many Requests` and a body of `{\"error\":\"usage quota exceeded\"}`.\n\nEach operation carries an `x-usage` extension describing the usage operation name and the number of credits it consumes, for example `\"x-usage\": {\"operation\": \"message.get\", \"credits\": 3}`. Requests are also rate-limited per IP (see `429`).\n\n## Error format\n\nNon-OK responses use a simple envelope:\n\n```json\n{\"error\": \"<message>\"}\n```"
  },
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Mailboxes",
      "description": "Create, list, fetch, and delete disposable mailboxes."
    },
    {
      "name": "Messages",
      "description": "List messages in a mailbox and fetch individual messages."
    },
    {
      "name": "Attachments",
      "description": "Download message attachments."
    },
    {
      "name": "Webhooks",
      "description": "Receive realtime HTTP callbacks when something happens on your mailboxes."
    }
  ],
  "security": [
    {
      "bearerAuth": []
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/api/v1/mailboxes": {
      "post": {
        "tags": ["Mailboxes"],
        "summary": "Create a mailbox",
        "description": "Creates a mailbox for the authenticated developer. The `username` field must be a full mailbox address on the configured mail domain (for example `dev-123@temp.mail.at`).",
        "operationId": "createMailbox",
        "x-usage": { "operation": "mailbox.create", "credits": 1, "category": "mailbox" },
        "security": [{ "bearerAuth": [] }],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/RequestEmail" }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "Mailbox created.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Mailbox" }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/BadRequest" },
          "401": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" },
          "409": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/Conflict" },
          "429": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/TooManyRequests" },
          "500": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/InternalServerError" }
        }
      },
      "get": {
        "tags": ["Mailboxes"],
        "summary": "List mailboxes",
        "description": "Lists all mailboxes owned by the authenticated developer.",
        "operationId": "listMailboxes",
        "x-usage": { "operation": "mailbox.list", "credits": 1, "category": "mailbox" },
        "security": [{ "bearerAuth": [] }],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Mailboxes owned by the developer.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Mailbox" }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized" },
          "429": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/TooManyRequests" },
          "500": { "$ref": "#/components/responses/InternalServerError" }
        }
      }
    },
